{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the best result so far at 0.619 acc / 0.610 F1, showing that multimodal fusion with concat adds ~2.8% over the best RNA-only setup (config_002, 0.591). The fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted) is the one design dimension in this otherwise-validated configuration that has not been tested. Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation when combining the (relatively weak) image features with the (strong) RNA features? If the image modality contributes a small but complementary signal, weighted fusion could down-weight it appropriately and avoid diluting the RNA signal; conversely, concat may already be sufficient. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable change from the current best configuration, directly exploiting the strongest evidence while testing an unexplored design axis. The expected performance delta is small but the information gain is high—ruling in or out weighted fusion lets us fix that dimension and focus remaining budget on larger-uncertainty choices (RNA encoder, image encoder) in subsequent experiments."
}

